course: dictionary
lesson: 13129
title: Folks: people, family and friends
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word folks is informal, which means it is used in friendly, everyday talk rather than in formal writing. Read the words around it to work out which meaning fits. «Folks round here are very friendly» means people who live nearby, because the sentence is about the people in the area.
explain: Sometimes folks means your parents or family. «I will ask my folks if I can stay late» tells you who is being asked: the child's parents. The word «my» is the clue. Ask yourself, who could the person be talking to or about?
explain: Folks can also be a friendly way to speak to a group, like a teacher saying «Hi, folks!» to a class. Folks is not really about a particular person here. It is a warm greeting, and it means "everyone."
fact: Folks means people, especially ordinary people, as in «Folks round here are friendly.»
fact: «My folks» means your parents or family, as in «I'll ask my folks.»
fact: «Hi, folks!» is a friendly way to speak to a group of people.
fact: Folk, used as an adjective, describes traditional music, stories and dances of ordinary people, as in «We sang folk songs.»
fact: Folks is informal, so it sounds friendly in speech and is less common in formal writing.
exercise: «Folks round here are very friendly.» What does folks mean? | Animals on the farm | *People who live in this area | Roads and trains | Trees and bushes
exercise: «I will ask my folks if I can stay late.» Who are my folks? | My teachers at school | A group of shopkeepers | Ordinary strangers in the street | *My parents and family
exercise: A teacher says, «Hi, folks! Let's start the lesson.» What is the teacher doing? | Asking for a pencil | *Greeting the whole group in a friendly way | Reading a sad poem | Telling the class off
test: «We learned a folk song about the sea.» What does folk mean in folk song? | Very new and modern | A kind of fish | A loud, fast drum | *Traditional music of ordinary people
test: «Old folks like to tell stories.» What does old folks mean? | Broken toys | *Elderly people | Empty houses | Old furniture
exam: Lily says, «My folks are picking me up at five.» Who is picking Lily up? | Her teacher | *Her parents or family | Her friends from school | A taxi driver
